      <h1 id="external-dns-operator-cluster-wide-proxy" class="group scroll-mt-20">Configuring the cluster-wide proxy on the External DNS Operator<a href="#external-dns-operator-cluster-wide-proxy" class="ml-2 text-muted-foreground opacity-0 group-hover:opacity-100 no-underline" aria-hidden="true" tabindex="-1">&para;</a></h1>
      <p>To propagate proxy settings to your deployed Operators, configure the cluster-wide proxy. The Operator Lifecycle Manager (OLM) automatically updates these Operators with the new <code>HTTP_PROXY</code>, <code>HTTPS_PROXY</code>, and <code>NO_PROXY</code> environment variables.</p>
      <h2 id="nw-configuring-cluster-wide-proxy_external-dns-operator-cluster-wide-proxy" class="group scroll-mt-20">Trusting the certificate authority of the cluster-wide proxy<a href="#nw-configuring-cluster-wide-proxy_external-dns-operator-cluster-wide-proxy" class="ml-2 text-muted-foreground opacity-0 group-hover:opacity-100 no-underline" aria-hidden="true" tabindex="-1">&para;</a></h2>
      <p class="_abstract">You can configure the External DNS Operator to trust the certificate authority of the cluster-wide proxy.</p>
      <p><strong>Procedure</strong></p>
      <ol>
      <li>
      Create the config map to contain the CA bundle in the <code>external-dns-operator</code> namespace by running the following command:
      <CodeBlock code={"$ oc -n external-dns-operator create configmap trusted-ca"} lang="terminal" />
      </li>
      <li>
      To inject the trusted CA bundle into the config map, add the <code>config.openshift.io/inject-trusted-cabundle=true</code> label to the config map by running the following command:
      <CodeBlock code={"$ oc -n external-dns-operator label cm trusted-ca config.openshift.io/inject-trusted-cabundle=true"} lang="terminal" />
      </li>
      <li>
      Update the subscription of the External DNS Operator by running the following command:
      <CodeBlock code={"$ oc -n external-dns-operator patch subscription external-dns-operator --type='json' -p='[{\"op\": \"add\", \"path\": \"/spec/config\", \"value\":{\"env\":[{\"name\":\"TRUSTED_CA_CONFIGMAP_NAME\",\"value\":\"trusted-ca\"}]}}]'"} lang="terminal" />
      </li>
      </ol>
      <p><strong>Verification</strong></p>
      <ul>
      <li>
      After deploying the External DNS Operator, verify that the trusted CA environment variable is added by running the following command. The output must show <code>trusted-ca</code> for the <code>external-dns-operator</code> deployment.
      <CodeBlock code={"$ oc -n external-dns-operator exec deploy/external-dns-operator -c external-dns-operator -- printenv TRUSTED_CA_CONFIGMAP_NAME"} lang="terminal" />
      </li>
      </ul>
    </article>
